      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CHIXFROMTHESTIX (2) bumped into a good one last start when no match, beaten 3.4L after starting this campaign in the Listed Max Simmonds Stakes. Pike hopping on board is a positive sign and the drop back to 1000m is no issue. Can go one better this time. GOD SHE'S GOOD (7) made a very tidy debut at Northam, closing into second after being hampered near the 150m. She was behind LUMINOUS LIL there, but with a better barrier and the race fitness under her belt, she makes plenty of appeal. SIP SOCIETY (8) is the unknown, but the Williams stable has the right debut profile, Chris Parnham rides, and two Lark Hill trials give her enough grounding to be treated as a serious threat. EXTREME MAKEOVER (6) has placed in both starts and was wide throughout when beaten half a length at Northam. Can make her presence felt. LUMINOUS LIL (3) didn't give anything else a chance last start and this shapes similarly.",
